claims:
1. A system for determining a status of a first user with respect to an object, said system comprising:
a fixed position device disposed in a fixed position relative to the object, said fixed position device including an antenna and configured to communicate wirelessly with a first portable device via a first communication link;
a locator processor configured to determine relative location information about the first portable device relative to the object, said locator processor configured to determine said relative location information about the first portable device based on a signal characteristic of communications wirelessly transmitted from the first portable device;
the locator processor configured to obtain absolute location information about the first portable device based on output from an absolute location system;
a tracking processor disposed on the object, the tracking processor configured to compare the relative location information and the absolute location information, the tracking processor operable, based on the comparison between the relative location information and the absolute location information, to determine the status of the first user corresponds to one of the following:
1) the first user entered the object at or proximal to a first location relative to the object;
2) the first user exited the object at or proximal to a second location relative to the object; and
3) the first user is at a third location different from the first location for entry and the second location for exit; and
the tracking processor operable to initiate a notification to the first user based on the status of the first user, wherein the notification is operable to prompt the first user to take corrective action based on the first user being at the third location different from the first location for entry and the second location for exit relative to the object.

11. A method for determining a status of a first user with respect to an object, said method comprising:
determining relative location information about a first device relative to the object based on a signal characteristic of communications wirelessly transmitted from the first device;
obtaining absolute location information about the first device based on output from an absolute location system;
comparing the relative location information and the absolute location information;
based on the comparison between the relative location information and the absolute location information, determining the status of the first user corresponds to one of the following:
1) the first user entered the object at or proximal to a first location relative to the object;
2) the first user exited the object at or proximal to a second location relative to the object; and
3) the first user is at a third location different from the first location for entry and the second location for exit; and
initiating a notification to the first user based on the status of the first user, wherein the notification is operable to prompt the first user to take corrective action based on the first user being at the third location different from the first location for entry and the second location for exit relative to the object.
